course: dictionary
lesson: 9079
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word slot is a good example. It can be a noun, a thing like an opening, or a verb, an action of putting something into place.
explain: «Picture a cash machine with something odd stuck on the card slot.» A card slot is a narrow opening where you push your card in. The words cash machine and card tell you the meaning is the opening, not a time.
explain: «Top athletes must tell testers where they will be for a 1-hour slot every day of the year.» Here a slot is a set time in a timetable, a time set aside for something. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about a place, a time, or an action? Then pick the meaning that fits.
fact: A slot can be a long, narrow opening where you put something in, like a coin.
fact: A slot can also be a place or time set aside in a list or timetable, like a time slot for an appointment.
fact: To slot something is to put it into a space where it fits, as in «slot in».
fact: Informally, in sport, «He slotted it into the net» means he scored neatly.
fact: Useful phrases: «coin slot», «time slot», «slot machine».
exercise: «Picture a cash machine with something odd stuck on the card slot.» What is a card slot? | A very loud noise | *A narrow opening where you push your card in | A time set aside for cards | A kind of game played with cards
exercise: «Top athletes must tell testers where they will be for a 1-hour slot every day.» What does slot mean here? | Someone who is very fast | *A set time in a timetable | A narrow hole in a wall | A way of putting shoes on
exercise: Nadia says, «I slot the last shape into the puzzle.» What does slot mean here? | To cook something slowly | *To put something into a space where it fits | To sing loudly | To lose something
test: «He slotted it into the net.» What does slotted mean here? | To drop it on the grass | To fall asleep | *To score neatly | To kick it hard and wide
test: Which phrase means a set time for an appointment? | Card hole | Coin slot | Slot blade | *Time slot
exam: «She will slot the new book onto the shelf.» What does slot mean here? | To score a goal in sport | A long, narrow opening | *To place it where it fits | A set time for a meeting
